  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">Output 2.3. Increased capacity of the ILO constituents to engage in a forward-looking international labour standards policy</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="FR">The Office received all article 22 reports on the following Conventions: C 6, C 17, C 26, C45, C81, C 88, C 98, C138 and C 182 within the deadline. The Office provided technical expertise in Portuguese to the Government for the preparation of its article 22 reports on the following Conventions: C 6, C 17, C 26, C45, C81, C 88, C 98, C138 and C 182.  Moreover, the Office organized a training on best practices on ILS reporting during the period 10 May 2021 - 2 July 2021, which was attended by two officials, from the Ministry of Labour and from the Ministry of Public Administration, responsible for international labour standards.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="FR">2.3.1. Percentage of reports on the application of ratified Conventions due by 1 September received in a timely manner that include replies to comments of the supervisory bodies</narrative>
    </title>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
    </period>
   </indicator>
  </result>
